---
import { crossfieldScenarios } from '../../data/crossfield-scenarios';
import ChapterOrnament from './ChapterOrnament.astro';
import RevisionComparison from './RevisionComparison.astro';
---
  <div class="revision-content">
    <ChapterOrnament section="queryable-definition-history" />
    <header>
      <h2 id="versions-heading">Measure how a proposed reporting definition changes the result.</h2>
      <p class="lede">A change in the numbers should be explainable. Retain the current definition, attach the proposed revision alongside it, and query both against the same source snapshot. Reviewers can see how much of the difference comes from the reporting rules before those rules reach production.</p>
    </header>
    {crossfieldScenarios.map((s, i) => <div id={`scenario-revision-${s.id}`} data-scenario-panel={s.id} hidden={i !== 0} role="region" aria-label={`${s.label} revision comparison`}>
      <RevisionComparison scenario={s} />
    </div>)}
    <div class="history-story">
      <div>
        <h3>Keep a queryable history of your reporting definitions.</h3>
        <p>Teams often need to explain a report long after its definition has changed. Keeping earlier versions lets you reopen the model that was used, read its rules, and compare its results with today’s definition using the same data. You can also test a proposed change this way before it reaches the reports your business relies on.</p>
        <p>Your application can keep those model versions and their validation results in a DuckDB database using Crossfield’s release store. Your team can choose which version new sessions use and select an earlier release if needed. People already using an attached model continue with that version.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="history-path" aria-label="Managed definition release history">
        <li><strong>Save each version</strong><span>Keep a copy of the rules used for reporting.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Compare the results</strong><span>Run both definitions against the same data.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Choose the version to use</strong><span>Adopt the tested definition and keep earlier versions available.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <p class="scope-note">Keep the model files yourself, or have your application manage them in the release store. <code>ATTACH</code> alone does not save a history. To reproduce an old report exactly, you also need the data, filters and query inputs used at the time. <a href="/products/crossfield/docs/model-versions">Read how model history works →</a></p>
    <details class="peer-comparison">
      <summary>How this compares with dbt, Cube and Snowflake</summary>
      <p>Version control is an established semantic-layer practice. Crossfield brings retained revisions into DuckDB as separately named catalogs, so SQL users can compare their results in one connection. The products below support change management through different workflows.</p>
      <div class="comparison-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Semantic model revision workflows" tabindex="0">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Product</th><th scope="col">Documented revision workflow</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Crossfield</th><td>Retain versioned packages and attach revisions side by side in DuckDB. An optional native release store keeps immutable published packages and validation records. <a href="/products/crossfield/docs/model-versions">Crossfield revision guide</a></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">dbt Semantic Layer</th><td>Develop metric definitions in a version-controlled dbt project. Deploy the semantic manifest and configure the Semantic Layer against a deployment environment. <a href="https://docs.getdbt.com/guides/sl-qs">dbt deployment guide</a></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Cube Cloud</th><td>Test model changes in an isolated development environment. Personal API endpoints follow the selected branch before changes are promoted to production. <a href="https://docs.cube.dev/docs/data-modeling/dev-mode">Cube development workflow</a></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Snowflake Semantic Views</th><td>Native database objects with YAML or SQL definitions kept in Git. Snowflake documents CI/CD, redeployment of earlier definitions and schema cloning for promotion. <a href="https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/views-semantic/best-practices-dev">Snowflake deployment practices</a></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">This compares documented workflows, not an exclusive claim to versioning or revision comparison. Reviewed October 27, 2026.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
<style>
  header { max-width:900px; }
  h2 { font-size:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3rem); line-height:1.15; }
  .lede { margin-top:1.25rem; font-size:1.1rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--color-soil-700); }
  a { color:var(--color-link); text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:4px; }
  [hidden] { display:none; }
  .history-story { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:4rem; margin-top:3rem; }
  .history-story h3 { font-size:clamp(1.65rem,2.5vw,2rem); line-height:1.25; }
  .history-story p { margin-top:1rem; color:var(--color-soil-700); font-size:.9375rem; line-height:1.8; }
  .history-path { list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0 0 0 1rem; }
  .history-path li { position:relative; padding:0 0 1.65rem 1.75rem; border-left:1px solid var(--color-field-700); }
  .history-path li::before { content:''; position:absolute; left:-6px; top:.35rem; width:11px; height:11px; background:var(--color-field-700); border:2px solid #fffdf7; border-radius:50%; }
  .history-path li:last-child { padding-bottom:0; border-color:transparent; }
  .history-path strong { display:block; font-weight:600; font-size:.9375rem; line-height:1.6; }
  .history-path span { display:block; margin-top:.3rem; font-size:.875rem; line-height:1.75; color:var(--color-soil-700); }
  .scope-note { margin-top:1.5rem; font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--color-soil-700); max-width:110ch; }
  .peer-comparison { margin-top:2rem; border-block:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); padding:1rem 0; }
  .peer-comparison summary { cursor:pointer; min-height:44px; align-content:center; color:var(--color-link); font-size:1rem; font-weight:500; }
  .peer-comparison summary:focus-visible,.comparison-scroll:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--color-link); outline-offset:4px; }
  .peer-comparison > p { margin-top:1rem; max-width:90ch; font-size:.9375rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--color-soil-700); }
  .comparison-scroll { overflow-x:auto; margin-top:1.5rem; }
  table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:.875rem; line-height:1.8; }
  th,td { text-align:left; vertical-align:top; padding:1rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); }
  thead th { padding-top:0; font-weight:600; }
  tbody th { width:22%; min-width:140px; font-weight:600; }
  td { min-width:250px; color:var(--color-soil-700); }
  td a { display:block; }
  .peer-comparison .comparison-note { font-size:.75rem; }
  @media(max-width:800px) { .history-story { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:2rem; } }
  @media(max-width:600px) { .history-path { padding-left:.5rem; } th,td { padding:.75rem; } }
</style>
